course: dictionary
lesson: 5358
title: Kinetic: the word for movement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Kinetic means about movement, or caused by movement. When you meet it, look at the words around it for clues, and ask: what is moving?
explain: «A rolling ball has kinetic energy.» The ball is moving, so kinetic must link to movement. The energy is the energy the ball has because it is rolling.
explain: «The faster or heavier an object moves, the more kinetic energy it has.» Speed and weight both make the amount bigger. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: moving things have more energy when they go faster or weigh more.
explain: Grown-ups sometimes use kinetic in a hidden way. «"Kinetic action" is US military jargon for a real attack with weapons that kills or destroys.» Fancy words can hide what really happens, so always ask what the words actually mean.
fact: Kinetic means about movement, or caused by movement.
fact: Kinetic energy is the energy an object has because it is moving.
fact: The faster or heavier something moves, the more kinetic energy it has.
fact: Kinetic art is art with parts that move.
fact: A ball held high has stored energy, called potential energy; as it falls, that energy turns into kinetic energy.
exercise: «A rolling ball has kinetic energy.» What does kinetic mean here? | About sleeping | About sounds | About colours | *About movement
exercise: What makes kinetic energy bigger? | Staying still | Being painted | *Moving faster | Being stored high up
exercise: Which is kinetic art? | A painting hung still on a wall | A book of poems | A photo of a sleeping cat | *Sculpture with parts that move in the wind
test: Wind turbines turn the kinetic energy of wind into what? | *Electricity | Paint | Silence | Sand
test: A ball held high has stored energy. What is that stored energy called? | Heat energy | Sound energy | Kinetic energy | *Potential energy
exam: In «"Kinetic action" is US military jargon for a real attack», what does kinetic action mean? | A broken machine | *A real attack with weapons | A slow walk | A peaceful dance
